# Deploy only through GitHub

Any deploy, upload, or ship to the production server goes through GitHub. Do not copy files onto the server by hand.

- Commit only the files that should go live, then push to `main`.
- Pushing `main` runs `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` on the self-hosted runner. That runs `deploy/scripts/deploy_release.sh`.
- The script copies added and modified files from that push onto `/opt/cashflow`. It does not delete server-only files. A portal file rebuilds the portal. A Python file recreates the API. A file in `cashflow_db/sql/` runs `python -m cashflow_db migrate`.
- Do not `scp`, `ssh` a file into `/opt/cashflow` or `/data/portal`, `docker cp` into the API, or recreate containers yourself.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials).
- Do not include unrelated local edits. Every file in the push overwrites the live copy.
- The committed file becomes the live file. Shared files must be the production version plus the change, not a local copy that drops server-only code.

```text
# deploy
git push origin main

# not a deploy
scp app.py abdu@server:/opt/cashflow/app.py
```
